<<<
2. Redundant negative after bud. But (now rare), but that (literary), & but what (colloq.), have often in negative & interrogative sentences the meaning that ...not.
===
**2. Redundant negative after *but*.** *But* (now rare), *but that* (literary), & *but what* (colloq.), have often in negative & interrogative sentences the meaning *that . . . not*.
>>>

<<<
But just as I shouldn't wonder if he didn't fall in is often heard in vulgar speech where didn't fall should fell, so careless writers insert after but the negative already implied in it.
===
But just as *I shouldn't wonder if he didn't fall in* is often heard in vulgar speech where *didn't fall* should be *fell*, so careless writers insert after *but* the negative already implied in it.
>>>

